  `-fsanitize=function` reports for the callbacks that Xt calls through cast
  function pointers are suppressed (`function:*`); all other checks stay on. A
  job `fuzz-replay` (also in `.ckgit/ci.yml`) runs
  `python3 cde/fuzz/run-fuzz.py --all --replay`. The fuzz runner has a new
  mode `--replay`, which runs every target once over every file of its corpus
  directory (libFuzzer `-runs=0`: no mutation) and exits 1 when an input
  crashes, and `--all`, which applies the action to every target. On Linux the
  compiler comes from `CLANG` (default: `clang` in PATH) and the X11
  headers and libraries from the system (`pkg-config`) instead of XQuartz; a
  target whose pkg-config modules are missing is skipped with a message.
