2026-11-13
- libDtSvc, found by fuzzing the type database reader and the cache file
  reader. Three defects are fixed. (1) A database file that began with
  `set DtDbVersion=` and a value longer than 12 bytes overran the heap: the
  version check expanded `$DtDbVersion` in a 13 byte copy, but
  `_DtDbFillVariables()` expects a buffer of `MAX_LINE_LENGTH` bytes. The
  copy now has that size, so a long version is expanded and the file is
  rejected with the message for an invalid version. (2) An invalid multibyte
  sequence in the name of a `set` line made `DefineVariable()` step back for
  ever (`mblen()` returned -1), and in the name of a `${...}` reference made
  `_DtDbFillVariables()` do the same. The sequence now ends the name. (3) The
  check of a type database cache file looked only at the indexes of its
  header; the string table, the integer tables, the records and the fields
  were trusted, so a damaged cache was read outside the mapped file. Before a
  cache is used, every table, count, index, string offset and chain is now
  checked to lie inside the file, and the strings to end inside it
  (`_DtShmValidateStrtab()`, `_DtShmValidateInttab()` and the new
  `cache_tables_valid()`); a cache that fails is ignored and rebuilt. The hash
  of a long name shifted by 32 bits or more (undefined behavior); the shift
  count now wraps at 32, which gives the hash values the hardware gave. Tests:
  `tests/check-dbreader-variables.py` and `tests/check-dtsmm-cache-bounds.py`,
  with the three inputs as seeds of the dtsvc-dbreader and dtsvc-mmcache fuzz
  targets.

2026-11-13
- DtHelp, dtlogin: three defects found by fuzzing. The attribute reader of the
  SDL parser (`_DtHelpCeGetSdlAttributeCdata()`) freed the caller's stack
  buffer when a number attribute had no closing quote or was cut off by the
  end of the file; it now frees only what it allocated, and reads the
  end-of-file value as an `int`. `_DtHelpCeGetSdlId()` dereferenced the
  missing string of an empty `id=""`; an empty id now fails like a missing
  one, and so do an empty enumeration or font value in `FormatSDL.c`, which
  also release the value on failure. The alias expansion of the dtlogin
  Xaccess reader repeated entries that were being expanded already and had
  no total limit, so aliases that list each other took exponential time; an
