2026-11-13
- dtexec, dtimsstart, dtpad: three programs ran non-async-signal-safe code
  from signal handlers. dtexec called ToolTalk (`tt_message_send()` and
  more) from the SIGINT handler: the handler now sets a flag and writes one
  byte to a self-pipe that the `select()` loop watches, and the loop runs the
  shutdown. dtimsstart ran `Exit()` (messages, `exit()`) from the termination
  handler and `put_xims_log()` and the whole wait cleanup (X calls) from the
  SIGCHLD handler: the handlers now record the signal, or reap the child and
  record its status, and wake the Xt loop with `XtNoticeSignal()`; the
  polling loop of the wait checks the records after every sleep. dtpad saved
  the edit sessions from the handler for every signal: the termination
  signals (HUP, INT, QUIT, PIPE, TERM) now run the save from the event loop
  through `XtAppAddSignal()`, while the fatal signals (ILL, ABRT, FPE, BUS,
  SEGV, SYS) keep a best-effort save in the handler that resets its own
  disposition, and a fault inside the save ends the process with `_exit()`
  instead of recursing. In all three, a second signal while the first is
  pending exits at once with `_exit()`. Tests:
  `programs/dtexec/tests/check-panic-signal.py`,
