2026-11-13
- dtlogin: the greeter ran its whole shutdown (closing the message catalog,
  restoring the bell, unsecuring the display, `XSync()`, closing the display)
  inside the SIGTERM handler, which can interrupt an X request in flight and
  corrupt the connection or deadlock. The handler now calls only
  `XtNoticeSignal()`, and `XtAppAddSignal()` runs the shutdown from the event
  loop; a second signal exits at once with `_exit()`. Before the toolkit exists
  the old sequence stays, since nothing else runs yet. Test:
